title: "GeoLineage: provenance for STAC-driven geospatial pipelines"
message: "If you use this software, study or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arzimanli
    given-names: Suad
    affiliation: "University of Łódź"
version: 2.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24428985
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/suadarzimanli/GeoLineage-Research"
url: "https://geolineage-research.pages.dev/"
keywords:
  - provenance
  - lineage
  - reproducibility
  - STAC
  - Earth observation
abstract: >-
  Lineage receipts, query-scoped diffs with reasons for every change, and reuse of
  unchanged outputs for pipelines built on STAC catalogs, implemented as a Python
  reference pipeline and a hosted Cloudflare/Supabase demo with identical identity
  rules, plus a study of 8,320 Sentinel-2 items from Earth Search and Planetary
  Computer on query stability, window churn, in-place updates, cross-catalog
  identity and reuse.
